    "Scratch marks belong to one optimization invocation on one immutable CFG. No semantic proof is cached or reused across graphs. Generation wrap clears all marks.",
    "All source, MBC, native Object and complete metadata bytes match between every subject, the independent screen and prior qualified fast runtime output. All four outputs also match for six complete array/enum and eight Bool/U64/I64/F64 checked scalar programs.",
    "1,048,576 graph/root/owner combinations compare exact DFS order with ordered sets, including cycles and repeated pending entries. Sparse block IDs and generation overflow are checked separately.",
    "Candidate peak RSS is higher with nonoverlapping ranges; no memory saving is claimed. Unchanged-stage elapsed variation is not attributed to visitation storage. Four compile observations are descriptive, not a statistical population.",
    "No new runtime-speed measurement campaign is claimed. Generated program bytes remain exactly identical, unlike the reverted SSA candidate whose runtime timing found slowdowns.",
    "The copied enum-state assembly provenance includes historical attempts, not a new fragment-only launch. Source, bytecode, Object and metadata comparisons all succeed on complete assembled programs.",
    "No grammar, language, generated-program behavior or backend optimization level change. Full compilation still exceeds ten seconds."
